// -----

// A handler-submit closure captured BY REFERENCE. `q.submit([&](handler& h){
// h.parallel_for(...) })` captures the enclosing `[&]` variables by reference,
// so the two USM pointers reach the device closure as `load(load(&local))`: the
// command-group functor is copied by value (a whole-struct load+store), the
// closure field holds `&local`, and the kernel dereferences it twice. This is
// the shape that severs the pointer from its malloc_device on the direct trace
// (the allocations live in the caller). Recovery follows the reference through
// the by-value aggregate copy back to each distinct allocation, so both fields
// are still proven distinct-USM and get noalias. Models the shape after the
// launch chain is collapsed into the caller.
